{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/839176-new-merit-exemplar-of-auspice","id":839176,"title":"[New Merit] Exemplar of Auspice","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-02-29T07:57:01-08:00","id":839176,"title":"[New Merit] Exemplar of Auspice","content":"Notably, I was reading through the Demon Translation Guide, and one of the new Merits within gave me a new idea. Any thoughts on this?<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Exemplar of (Auspice) (\u2022)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>Prerequisites:</b>Werewolf, must possess an Auspice</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">All Uratha gain some extra ability in the Skills governed by their Auspice when they undergo their first change, but you have discovered a natural talent for your role. </span></span><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">You now gain an Exceptional Success with three successes instead of five when making a roll involving your Auspice Skills.</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-29T08:07:50-08:00","id":839182,"title":"","content":"Make it two dots and attach it to to a single skill that you've already purchased Moon-Kissed for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":717,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","user":"Monghani","date":". 02-29-2016, 11:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","name":"Monghani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar717_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-29T08:19:37-08:00","id":839188,"title":"","content":"I don't like it. It's too broad/general and overlaps with other stuff. It basically gives character a persistent Inspired condition for just 1 dot and without any previous roll. I would personally change it to Primal Urge times per lunar month or to +X dice on a roll with some Drawback like having to fulfill minor Ban condition. <br /> <br /> Look also at Inspiring<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"> (\u2022\u2022\u2022) merit. It applies to other people and not to self, but it gives Inspired condition once and after successful roll first, also requires you to have 3 Presence and buy 3 dot merit. Compared to it buying 1 dot merit with ceaseless Inspired condition to 2 skills (not sources of inspiration) feels overpowered. </span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7871-miriander","name":"Miriander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-29T08:47:28-08:00","id":839212,"title":"","content":"@Monghani<br /> @Miriander<br /> I was afraid of that. Give me some time and I'll try to make something better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-29T09:07:34-08:00","id":839231,"title":"","content":"Needs a drawback. Like picking an auspice skill, then the other 2 don't benefit from 10 again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-29T11:32:08-08:00","id":839327,"title":"","content":"I'd go the route of furthering the drawback of Moon-kissed. The Non-Auspice Skill you have dots and chose for it permanently suffers a -1 penalty. Basically, the idea is to make you more iconic in the role Luna chose for you. But less so in things outside of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","name":"Monghani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar717_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-29T11:37:38-08:00","id":839330,"title":"","content":"At that point how is it different from Moon-Kissed?<br /> <br /> MOON-KISSED (\u2022)<br /> Prerequisites: Auspice Skill at \u2022\u2022 or higher<br /> Effect: Your character\u2019s auspice affects her more than most. When taking this Merit, choose one of her three auspice Skills. That Skill has the 9-again quality. If you already have 9-again available, use 8-again. When her auspice moon is visible, spending Willpower gives +4 dice to rolls using that Skill instead of +3. <br /> You can take this Merit multiple times, reflecting different auspice Skills.<br /> Drawback: When taking this Merit, choose a non-auspice <br /> Skill your character has dots in. Rolls requiring that Skill do not benefit from the 10-again quality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}